[--germinate
  [ph-alvo'the emitted format is being replaced by glyph-package, and the parser discards the operator that the new format exists to record']
  [ph-esforco'carry the operator from the lexer to the XML, derive the golden from the specification, rederive the vectors, gate before emitter, decide the inverse, rewrite the reference, republish the skill']
  [ph-ramo'the five examples, pure glyph plus verified engine output']
  [ph-ramo'BUNDLE_TARGET.md, the specification for the six layers']
  [ph-ramo'XML_REFERENCE.md lines 99 to 101, where extend, comma and divide are documented']
  [ph-ramo'chainElement in glyph-parser.js, the marker the engine computes and never serialises']
  [ph-limite'out of scope: the six-layer bundle emitters, the agent file writer, the _ORBITAL runtime, the RAG retrieval engine']
  [ph-trava'the operator reaches the XML before any chain element is emitted, and the golden derives from the specification, never from an implementation']
  [ph-fruto'a compiler whose emitted format records the operator it was given, and whose inverse returns what went in']
  [ph-suposicao'the language sweep rides in this release, because the vectors, the reference and both skills are already being rewritten']
  [ph-criterio'the four guarantees the current XML makes: editorial force, block segmentation, needs, and exact string fidelity']
];
